        "evidence_snippet": "The XPS survey spectrum clearly suggests that the film mainly consists of only two elements: W and O (Supplementary Fig. 4). Specifically, the W 4f core-level XPS spectrum can be deconvoluted into two doublets (W^6+, W^5+) with atomic percentages of W^5+ and W^6+ fitted to be 11.6% and 88.4%, indicating the presence of mixed tungsten states in the film (Supplementary Fig. 5)."
